<p begin="00:50:58.866" end="00:51:00.300" style="s2">For five years,</p>
<p begin="00:51:00.600" end="00:51:03.933" style="s2">Mr. Calloway kept that orchard running all by himself.</p>
<p begin="00:51:08.833" end="00:51:10.000" style="s2">I didn&#39;t run off.</p>
<p begin="00:51:11.000" end="00:51:12.200" style="s2">I was put on a train.</p>
<p begin="00:51:14.533" end="00:51:16.733" style="s2">Sixty-eight thousand for a new tractor.</p>
<p begin="00:51:17.666" end="00:51:19.800" style="s2">The red tractor parked by our barn is</p>
<p begin="00:51:19.800" end="00:51:21.500" style="s2">the same one I learned to drive on.</p>
<p begin="00:51:26.033" end="00:51:27.933" style="s2">Harold Bixby, four hundred hours of picking.</p>
<p begin="00:51:30.466" end="00:51:32.733" style="s2">Harold passed four years ago.</p>
<p begin="00:51:33.133" end="00:51:34.633" style="s2">I was at his funeral.</p>
<p begin="00:51:39.133" end="00:51:41.200" style="s2">So was I. I sang.</p>
<p begin="00:51:45.633" end="00:51:48.900" style="s2">Invoice eighty-three nineteen, paid twice. Three hundred</p>
<p begin="00:51:48.933" end="00:51:51.733" style="s2">thousand to Larkspur, a company run by the buyer&#39;s own executive.</p>
<p begin="00:51:51.733" end="00:51:56.466" style="s2">And a letter from Cole Hotel Group, ending</p>
<p begin="00:51:56.466" end="00:51:58.266" style="s2">the deal because the seller&#39;s numbers were false.</p>
<p begin="00:51:59.333" end="00:52:00.833" style="s2">Bookkeeping errors, Your Honor. She</p>
<p begin="00:52:01.433" end="00:52:03.733" style="s2">used to make change at a roadside stand.</p>
<p begin="00:52:05.300" end="00:52:07.700" style="s2">With my mother. Every Sunday.</p>
<p begin="00:52:08.733" end="00:52:10.466" style="s2">That&#39;s how I know what the stand made.</p>
<p begin="00:52:12.066" end="00:52:13.800" style="s2">Petitioner calls Brett Mercer.</p>
<p begin="00:52:26.666" end="00:52:31.300" style="s2">Walt owed a lot of money. To a casino in Battle Creek.</p>
<p begin="00:52:32.500" end="00:52:34.666" style="s2">He had to sell before she turned twenty-five.</p>
<p begin="00:52:34.933" end="00:52:37.100" style="s2">He paid me ten thousand to marry</p>
<p begin="00:52:37.100" end="00:52:39.000" style="s2">her and promised me forty more after closing.</p>
<p begin="00:52:40.433" end="00:52:43.100" style="s2">Your Honor, these are text messages from Mr.</p>
<p begin="00:52:43.100" end="00:52:45.066" style="s2">Calloway&#39;s phone to Mr. Mercer&#39;s.</p>
<p begin="00:52:51.466" end="00:52:53.000" style="s2">&quot;Get her to sign at the wedding.&quot;</p>
<p begin="00:52:54.466" end="00:52:55.733" style="s2">&quot;Don&#39;t let her call anyone.&quot;</p>
<p begin="00:52:56.666" end="00:52:58.400" style="s2">&quot;Don&#39;t let her back till closing.&quot;</p>
<p begin="00:52:59.500" end="00:53:02.033" style="s2">I paid you to get rid of her, not to—</p>
<p begin="00:53:02.066" end="00:53:04.866" style="s2">Mr. Calloway. Sit down.</p>
<p begin="00:53:13.200" end="00:53:15.700" style="s2">This court finds that the beneficiary&#39;s consent</p>
<p begin="00:53:15.700" end="00:53:18.133" style="s2">and power of attorney were obtained by fraud.</p>
<p begin="00:53:18.266" end="00:53:19.200" style="s2">Both are void.</p>
<p begin="00:53:22.033" end="00:53:24.000" style="s2">Walter Calloway is removed as</p>
<p begin="00:53:24.000" end="00:53:26.066" style="s2">trustee, effective immediately.</p>
<p begin="00:53:27.300" end="00:53:29.466" style="s2">Ivy Calloway will serve as trustee</p>
<p begin="00:53:29.466" end="00:53:31.800" style="s2">until the trust ends in October.</p>
<p begin="00:53:32.300" end="00:53:34.600" style="s2">All records go to the county prosecutor.</p>
<p begin="00:53:38.500" end="00:53:39.233" style="s2">Walter Calloway,</p>
<p begin="00:53:39.233" end="00:53:40.733" style="s2">you&#39;re under arrest for embezzlement.</p>
<p begin="00:53:46.000" end="00:53:47.300" style="s2">You shouldn&#39;t have come back.</p>
<p begin="00:53:47.466" end="00:53:49.700" style="s2">This is my mother&#39;s land. I&#39;m home.</p>
<p begin="00:53:57.433" end="00:53:59.200" style="s2">You were right about one thing, Brett.</p>
<p begin="00:53:59.900" end="00:54:03.033" style="s2">I don&#39;t belong in your world. Thank God.</p>
<p begin="00:54:14.570" end="00:54:15.770" style="s2">The transfer&#39;s in.</p>
<p begin="00:54:16.590" end="00:54:18.590" style="s2">A hundred and eighty-six thousand.</p>
<p begin="00:54:18.600" end="00:54:20.000" style="s2">The default is cured,</p>
<p begin="00:54:20.233" end="00:54:22.133" style="s2">and tomorrow&#39;s auction is canceled.</p>
<p begin="00:54:22.700" end="00:54:24.266" style="s2">The rest of the loan goes back</p>
<p begin="00:54:24.266" end="00:54:25.500" style="s2">to regular monthly payments.</p>
<p begin="00:54:36.433" end="00:54:37.700" style="s2">The judge signed it.</p>
<p begin="00:54:37.866" end="00:54:39.100" style="s2">Your marriage is void.</p>
<p begin="00:54:39.466" end="00:54:40.933" style="s2">Legally, you were never his wife.</p>
<p begin="00:54:45.200" end="00:54:47.000" style="s2">Best birthday present I&#39;ve ever gotten.</p>
<p begin="00:54:48.033" end="00:54:49.066" style="s2">Happy twenty-fifth.</p>
<p begin="00:54:49.300" end="00:54:50.433" style="s2">The trust ends today,</p>
<p begin="00:54:50.433" end="00:54:51.933" style="s2">so the orchard&#39;s in your name.</p>
<p begin="00:54:55.600" end="00:54:57.633" style="s2">And Brett was sentenced in Chicago.</p>
<p begin="00:54:57.833" end="00:55:01.066" style="s2">He pleaded guilty to theft and conspiracy. Probation,</p>
<p begin="00:55:01.100" end="00:55:03.233" style="s2">and he pays back every cent he took from you.</p>
<p begin="00:55:04.300" end="00:55:06.000" style="s2">The detective dropped this off.</p>
<p begin="00:55:16.666" end="00:55:17.733" style="s2">My own savings,</p>
<p begin="00:55:18.133" end="00:55:20.533" style="s2">plus a small business loan. In my name.</p>
<p begin="00:55:23.400" end="00:55:24.866" style="s2">Your credit line&#39;s paid off.</p>
<p begin="00:55:25.466" end="00:55:27.300" style="s2">Cole&#39;s first payment came through in August.</p>
<p begin="00:55:28.300" end="00:55:29.633" style="s2">That&#39;s the letter from the bank.</p>
<p begin="00:55:35.600" end="00:55:37.633" style="s2">The day you walked into my café,</p>
<p begin="00:55:37.800" end="00:55:39.233" style="s2">you were asking for work.</p>
<p begin="00:55:39.633" end="00:55:41.500" style="s2">Now you&#39;ve got a door of your own.</p>
<p begin="00:55:43.333" end="00:55:45.300" style="s2">Because you never stopped believing in me.</p>
<p begin="00:55:46.400" end="00:55:47.733" style="s2">One double espresso.</p>
<p begin="00:55:49.066" end="00:55:49.900" style="s2">At this hour?</p>
<p begin="00:55:55.000" end="00:55:58.000" style="s2">Or... one yes.</p>
<p begin="00:56:01.333" end="00:56:02.700" style="s2">Before I answer, there&#39;s something you need to know.</p>
<p begin="00:56:03.533" end="00:56:04.633" style="s2">Maggie is my mom.</p>
<p begin="00:56:05.466" end="00:56:06.433" style="s2">Not by blood.</p>
<p begin="00:56:07.100" end="00:56:08.266" style="s2">But she&#39;s my mom.</p>
<p begin="00:56:09.400" end="00:56:10.900" style="s2">Wherever I live, she lives.</p>
<p begin="00:56:12.500" end="00:56:13.900" style="s2">Then she&#39;s my mom too.</p>
<p begin="00:56:14.800" end="00:56:16.033" style="s2">Our home is her home.</p>
<p begin="00:56:17.500" end="00:56:18.300" style="s2">Yes.</p>
<p begin="00:56:20.466" end="00:56:23.500" style="s2">My kids. Oh, my kids.</p>
<p begin="00:56:32.033" end="00:56:34.900" style="s2">I now pronounce you husband and wife.</p>
<p begin="00:56:43.000" end="00:56:45.133" style="s2">Mom. Come stand with us.</p>
<p begin="00:56:46.200" end="00:56:48.800" style="s2">I lost a daughter once. And look...</p>
<p begin="00:56:49.600" end="00:56:51.000" style="s2">life gave me another one.</p>
</div>
</body>
</tt>
